A||||19||My7Fieros||AAARRRGGG!!!! WHAT A SH*TTY NIGHT!!!||||8||
Z||000000||My7Fieros||10-07-2001||04:57 AM||||Ok, like Cheever's bad mood, I had one tonight. Here what happened. I get to work and after roll call they're issuing equipment (radios, shotguns, flashlights, blah blah blah). Im the last person to get equipment and they run out of radios (the portable kind worn on the duty belt w/ the shoulder mike)....ok, no biggie. My LT. tells me he'll get me one from a day shift person comming in and he'll give it to me in an hour or so....ok(and he did). <BR>Well after being in service for about 2 hours I get the call everyone there hates to get....a prisoner has to go to the hospital for some reason (stomach pains or something)..and when an inmate goes to the hospital, the sheriff wants a deputy to stay there w/ him (for security reasons). Well, guess who gets stuck w/ that job tonight!    <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/mad.gif"> Its a BORING suck ass assignment...standing or sitting there in a hospital room for hours on end...ZZZZZZZZZZZZZZZZZZZZZ. Needless to say I was none to happy to get that call, knowing I was going to undoubtably spend the rest of the shift there (and of course I did). But wait! It gets better.....<BR>When I get to the jail to pick up this turd to take him to the hospital (and baby sit his dumb ass) there was an inmate there giving the jailors a hard time...to say the least. Well this guy and a jailor are in a room off to the side and I can hear them yelling and starting to fight. SH!T....here we go....I go to yank open the door and right at that time the jailor sprays the inmate (with the pepper spray, only this stuff is much worse)....guess who gets a direct shot of this stuff in the face....yup, me! Sigh, ok..after all this crap, I take the guy to my squad car (the guy Im taking to the hospital) and when I go to open the door I realize I locked my keys in the car.    <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/mad.gif">...I have to call a car from a neighboring city police to come and use a slim jim to "break in" to my squad car. Needless to say the prisoner and the city officer thought that was the funniest thing they'd ever seen.   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/rolleyes.gif"> oh well..Im tired now, its been an "interesting" night.<BR>Well, I guess its time to get off my soapbox..thanx for listening to my b!tch.<P>------------------<BR><FONT SIZE="3"><FONT COLOR="blue"><B><I>My 7 Fieros</FONT></FONT></B></I><P>[This message has been edited by My7Fieros (edited 10-07-2001).]<p>[This message has been edited by My7Fieros (edited 10-07-2001).]||||reg||8
Z||000001||fierohoho||10-07-2001||06:21 AM||||Wow, thats rough.<P>Stuff like that is why I like the small department I work for.<P>My equipment (flashlight,radio, ect...) goes home with me.<P>I get a take home squad which only I drive, it's a life of luxury.<P>The Deputies take care of the prisoners after I turn them over to jail staff.<P>So far an easy weekend, two speeders, one domestic, one prowler call, and a DWI arrest,(he was at a .16 BAC).<P>The way I see it you had a boring shift but the best part...no paperwork <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><P>I'm on Pennock's to keep from doing my paperwork which I will most likely have done before 0600 so I don't have it hanging over my head on Sunday night.<P>Work safe, HoHo<P>------------------<BR>'84 SE 2.5l<BR>'85 Coupe 2.5l now getting a 3800<BR>'86 SE 2.5l<BR>       <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/lightbar.gif"> ||||reg||1
Z||000002||fierobaby||10-07-2001||11:34 AM||||wow! that must have sucked... I had a pretty good night but I feel for you... *HUG* being a cop is tough work||||reg||1
Z||000003||maryjane||10-07-2001||11:55 AM||||Sounds like a rough nite alright. I recently had a need to call 911 for police help. They were here in a couple of minutes, in force. Stayed till it was resolved (about 3 hrs) and one officer stopped by the next day to see how things turned out. You'll never see me make a dumb donut shop joke again. Be safe guys.||||reg||14
Z||000004||Joe4x4||10-07-2001||12:13 PM||||&lt;salute&gt;......on the job...... <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">||||reg||1
Z||000005||FieroHeather||10-07-2001||12:14 PM||||Wow dude... Murphy's Law in action.  Bummer.  Do ya at least get some of this Turkey weekend off at all?  Maybe some time with friends/family members may help you start off the upcoming week a little better.<P>Murphy's Law is my life's theme  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/rolleyes.gif"><P><sub>Edited to fix da mistakes...figures I'd make a mistake in this post!</sub><p>[This message has been edited by FieroHeather (edited 10-07-2001).]|||65.92.82.218||reg||1
